---
/**
 * Hero. The card on the right is an illustrative example of a synthesized
 * brief — labelled as such, because the site ships no customer screenshots.
 */
---

<section
  id="hero"
  class="relative px-6 pb-20 pt-32 sm:pt-36 lg:pb-28 lg:pt-44"
>
  <div
    class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-center gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[1.05fr_0.95fr] lg:gap-20"
  >
    <div>
      <p
        class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-pz-clay-strong"
      >
        Parenting decision support
      </p>
      <h1
        class="mt-5 font-heading text-4xl font-semibold leading-[1.08] sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl"
      >
        The parenting app that thinks with you — in your own AI, or ours.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-pz-ink-soft">
        Parenza keeps a structured record of your family, puts a panel of
        specialist agents to work on it — feeding, sleep, medical, education,
        money — and returns one synthesized answer instead of five conflicting
        ones.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-9 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-center">
        <a
          href="#early-access"
          class="inline-flex h-13 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-pz-clay-strong px-8 py-4 text-base font-semibold text-white transition-colors hover:bg-pz-clay-strong-hover"
          >Request early access</a
        >
        <a
          href="#how-it-works"
          class="inline-flex h-13 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-pz-line-strong px-8 py-4 text-base font-medium text-pz-ink transition-colors hover:border-pz-ink-mute hover:bg-pz-sand"
          >See how it works</a
        >
      </div>

      <p class="mt-5 text-sm text-pz-ink-mute">
        A tracker records what happened. Parenza tells you what to do about it —
        and shows its reasoning.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Illustrative brief card -->
    <div class="relative">
      <div
        aria-hidden="true"
        class="pointer-events-none absolute -inset-6 -z-10 rounded-[2rem] bg-pz-clay-wash opacity-70 blur-2xl"
      >
      </div>

      <figure
        class="overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-pz-line bg-pz-paper shadow-[0_24px_60px_-32px_rgba(43,37,33,0.45)]"
      >
        <div
          class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-pz-line bg-pz-sand px-5 py-3"
        >
          <span
            class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-pz-ink-soft"
            >Chief of Staff · morning brief</span
          >
          <span class="text-xs text-pz-ink-mute">Tue 07:10</span>
        </div>

        <div class="px-5 py-6 sm:px-7">
          <p
            class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-pz-clay-strong"
          >
            TL;DR
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-pz-ink">
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span
                class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-pz-clay"
                aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span
                >Night wakings are up on the last three days, but total intake is
                flat — this looks like the 4-month change, not underfeeding.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span
                class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-pz-clay"
                aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span
                >Hold the current routine for three more nights before changing
                anything. One change at a time, or you won't know what worked.</span
              >
            </li>
          </ul>

          <p
            class="mt-6 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-pz-clay-strong"
          >
            Recommended
          </p>
          <ol
            class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-pz-ink-soft"
          >
            <li>1. Keep the bedtime window as it is until Friday.</li>
            <li>2. Log the wakings — we'll compare against this week.</li>
            <li>
              3. Six-week check is due: bring the growth entries with you.
            </li>
          </ol>

          <div
            class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-t border-pz-line pt-5"
          >
            <span class="text-xs text-pz-ink-mute">Informed by</span>
            <span
              class="rounded-full bg-pz-sage-wash px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-pz-sage-strong"
              >Sleep</span
            >
            <span
              class="rounded-full bg-pz-sage-wash px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-pz-sage-strong"
              >Feeding</span
            >
            <span
              class="rounded-full bg-pz-sage-wash px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-pz-sage-strong"
              >Medical</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>

      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-center text-xs text-pz-ink-mute">
        Illustrative example of a synthesized brief — not a real family's data.
      </figcaption>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
